{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a5a8140963272729", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# SemaVoice: Semantic-Aware Continuous Autoregressive Speech Synthesis\narXiv: 2605.16964\nAuthors: Huimeng Wang, Hui Lu, Jiajun Deng, Haoning Xu, Youjun Chen, Xueyuan Chen, Zhaoqing Li, Shuhai Peng, Shiyin Kang, Xunying Liu\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We present SemaVoice, a semantic-aware continuous autoregressive modeling framework that enables effective unified modeling of high-level semantic-prosodic planning and fine-grained acoustic rendering for high-fidelity zero-shot TTS.\n  2. We identify the mismatch between reconstruction-driven continuous speech representations and semantic-prosodic modeling as a key bottleneck in continuous autoregressive TTS, and introduce an SFM-guided alignment mechanism that enhances semantic coherence by aligning continuous representations with high-level semantic and prosodic information encoded in speech foundation models, improving generation robustness without modifying the downstream TTS architecture or training pipeline.\n  3. We validate SemaVoice through large-scale training on 150K hours of bilingual speech, achieving competitive performance compared with state-of-the-art open-source zero-shot TTS systems in both objective and subjective evaluations.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/架构-NAR-Diffusion", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "779e1967-e735-49f9-b3db-e546588afbfa", "uuid": "deeee80b-646f-4773-9f61-45308ccc91b7", "timestamp": "2026-08-10T07:10:43.728Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# SemaVoice: Semantic-Aware Continuous Autoregressive Speech Synthesis\narXiv: 2605.16964\nAuthors: Huimeng Wang, Hui Lu, Jiajun Deng, Haoning Xu, Youjun Chen, Xueyuan Chen, Zhaoqing Li, Shuhai Peng, Shiyin Kang, Xunying Liu\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We present SemaVoice, a semantic-aware continuous autoregressive modeling framework that enables effective unified modeling of high-level semantic-prosodic planning and fine-grained acoustic rendering for high-fidelity zero-shot TTS.\n  2. We identify the mismatch between reconstruction-driven continuous speech representations and semantic-prosodic modeling as a key bottleneck in continuous autoregressive TTS, and introduce an SFM-guided alignment mechanism that enhances semantic coherence by aligning continuous representations with high-level semantic and prosodic information encoded in speech foundation models, improving generation robustness without modifying the downstream TTS architecture or training pipeline.\n  3. We validate SemaVoice through large-scale training on 150K hours of bilingual speech, achieving competitive performance compared with state-of-the-art open-source zero-shot TTS systems in both objective and subjective evaluations.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/架构-NAR-Diffusion", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-bbf40e8a5e26244c", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# VoxCPM: Tokenizer-Free TTS for Context-Aware Speech Generation and True-to-Life Voice Cloning\narXiv: 2509.24650\nAuthors: Yixuan Zhou, Guoyang Zeng, Xin Liu, Xiang Li, Renjie Yu, Ziyang Wang, Runchuan Ye, Weiyue Sun, Jiancheng Gui, Kehan Li, Zhiyong Wu, Zhiyuan Liu\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose an end-to-end hierarchical architecture that introduces an internal semi-discrete bottleneck to resolve the expressivity-stability trade-off by implicitly separating semantic-prosodic planning from fine-grained acoustic modeling.\n  2. We introduce a residual learning strategy that achieves functional specialization without architectural fragmentation, eliminating dependency on external speech tokenizers and simplifying the training pipeline.\n  3. We demonstrate the efficacy of our approach through large-scale training on 1.8 million hours of bilingual speech, achieving state-of-the-art zero-shot TTS performance among open-source systems with high inference efficiency.\n  4. We provide extensive ablation studies validating the semi-discrete residual representations as crucial for robust and expressive synthesis, and publicly release the code and models to support community development.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Diffusion, TTS/控制-参考语音, 压缩, 压缩/量化-FSQ", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "779e1967-e735-49f9-b3db-e546588afbfa", "uuid": "8a06b75d-148b-4df2-a304-db8969c5537c", "timestamp": "2026-08-10T07:10:43.994Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# VoxCPM: Tokenizer-Free TTS for Context-Aware Speech Generation and True-to-Life Voice Cloning\narXiv: 2509.24650\nAuthors: Yixuan Zhou, Guoyang Zeng, Xin Liu, Xiang Li, Renjie Yu, Ziyang Wang, Runchuan Ye, Weiyue Sun, Jiancheng Gui, Kehan Li, Zhiyong Wu, Zhiyuan Liu\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose an end-to-end hierarchical architecture that introduces an internal semi-discrete bottleneck to resolve the expressivity-stability trade-off by implicitly separating semantic-prosodic planning from fine-grained acoustic modeling.\n  2. We introduce a residual learning strategy that achieves functional specialization without architectural fragmentation, eliminating dependency on external speech tokenizers and simplifying the training pipeline.\n  3. We demonstrate the efficacy of our approach through large-scale training on 1.8 million hours of bilingual speech, achieving state-of-the-art zero-shot TTS performance among open-source systems with high inference efficiency.\n  4. We provide extensive ablation studies validating the semi-discrete residual representations as crucial for robust and expressive synthesis, and publicly release the code and models to support community development.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Diffusion, TTS/控制-参考语音, 压缩, 压缩/量化-FSQ", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
